/**
 * NEOFFICE FILE — Swiss-French (Suisse romande) terminology overrides.
 * Owned 100% by Neoservice. Not from upstream OCE.
 * Created: 2026-06-25
 *
 * WHY a `languageChanged` listener (and not a one-shot merge like
 * swiss-pack/i18n.ts): these overrides reuse EXISTING keys (`boq.title`,
 * `takeoff.*`, `assemblies.type_*`) that the bundled `app/locales/fr.ts`
 * chunk ALSO defines. That chunk lazy-loads with
 * `addResourceBundle(..., overwrite=true)` (see `app/i18n.ts`) AFTER boot and
 * then emits `languageChanged`. A boot-time merge would therefore be
 * clobbered. By re-applying on every `languageChanged` — which fires right
 * after each `fr.ts` merge — our Swiss terms always land on top. No upstream
 * file is edited, so an OCE update can never overwrite this layer.
 *
 * Validated glossary (Cédric Protti, rdv 2026-06-24): BOQ / DQE / bordereau
 * → Devis ; Section → Chapitre ; Takeoff / Métré → Prémétré ; the cost-element
 * types → Matériaux / Main-d’œuvre / Machines / Outillage / Tiers. KEPT as-is:
 * Assemblage, Position, Catalogue.
 */
